      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T18:21:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t always assert ec reset, because RMA centers don\u0027t want the board to reset after they do RMA open. We need to have a way to wipe the TPM without resetting the AP. tpm_stop ensures the AP can\u0027t use the TPM even though it\u0027s still up.\n\nWe were asserting EC_RST_L before, so I thought we should keep that. I\u0027m fine with removing both.\nassert_ec_rst doesn\u0027t work very quickly on Mistral, so I thought tpm_stop would guarantee the tpm is stopped even if the AP doesn\u0027t stop.\n\nI thought adding tpm_stop is pretty harmless, because tpm_reset_request should clear it quickly. It just guarantees the TPM can\u0027t be used.",
      "parentUuid": "862ac879_6a62488e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 238,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 245,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "98b1e204a08ac4655cbcf79f1c666111ea9cba7c",
